# Kept out of the deployment.
#
# Vercel's builder typechecks the TypeScript it finds, with its own compiler
# rather than ours — and it found the test suite, which `tsconfig.json`
# excludes and which therefore had never been checked by that compiler. A type
# error in a test failed the deploy of an application the test is not part of.
#
# Tests do not belong in a serverless bundle regardless. They are still run by
# `npm test`, and still typechecked deliberately: see tsconfig.vercelcheck.json.
tests/

# One-off maintenance scripts. Same reason as the tests above: Vercel's builder
# typechecks whatever TypeScript it finds, with its own compiler and its own
# settings, and it reads neither our tsconfig nor its module mode. The
# WordPress import uses `import.meta.dirname`, which that compiler rejects
# outright when it decides the output is CommonJS.
#
# The .js files here are deliberately not excluded — `npm run build` calls
# copy-assets.js and bundle.js.
#
# Typechecked deliberately, like the tests: tsconfig.vercelcheck.json.
scripts/*.ts
scripts/wp-media-map.json
